  "note": [
    "Booth 2's fabric (DR-106), cut from the one Kalamontee layout in scripts/fabric-kalamontee.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. BOOTH-2.metadata.json v6: 4.2 x 3.2 x 3.4, the eye at the middle; one doorless 1.5 x 2.5 opening west, which WEST and OUT both name (compone.zil 2717-2718). \"This is a tiny room with a large \\\"2\\\" painted on the wall. A panel contains a slot about ten centimeters wide, a brown button labelled \\\"1\\\" and a tan button labelled \\\"3.\\\"\" (compone.zil 2710-2712).",
    "The numeral on the east (back) wall, 0.7 x 1.2. The panel on the north wall, 0.5 x 0.45 (globals.CONTROLS): the sign strip at the top, dark, lit on READY (TELEPORTATION-ON == true) as the one switch here; the slot under it; the brown 1 over the tan 3. One ceiling fitting.",
    "West through the mouth, on the one axis: the Elevator Lobby's floor, its ceiling with the middle and far pairs of its lamps, its west wall 14.26 m out and in the middle of it the Corridor Junction mouth; through that the Junction's floor with the dead walkway's end, its west wall and the Long Hall mouth, fully in view, and the hall running off into the dark. NOT the elevator doors: the lobby's side walls stand 5 m off the axis, which the cone reaches only past the lobby's far wall, so neither door, button nor side wall is in sight, and they are drawn shut as every other scene draws them."
